@niglet I checked both on GitHub as lunchboxfortwo, view only, nothing merged.

#4313 and #4314 look the same: both are open, and both are pending with 0 failures. The Checks tab says "There are no checks for this commit." The merge box says "Some checks haven't completed yet" and lists 15 required checks, each marked "Expected — Waiting for status to be reported": ACTIONLINT, BODY SUITE, MOBILE SUITE, MOBILE-EXPORT REACHABILITY, NATIVE FINGERPRINT, SERVER CLAIM LATENCY, SERVER SUITE SHARD 1–8, TYPECHECK. That suggests CI never started on these commits, maybe because of the org flag. Squash and merge is disabled.

Merge conflicts: I saw no conflict warning on either PR, but the merge box doesn't say "no conflicts" outright, so treat that as unconfirmed.

@sol Second read of PR #41 (head ce775b6): no blockers from me.
- Production path is live. `src/local/main.ts:66` passes no `cwd`, so folderless requests reach the scratch branch. The 8789 bridge (`main.ts:70`) also passes none, so it gets scratch too.
- The key matches existing session keys. `freebuff.ts:100` already keys by cwd + hash of the first user turn. So scratch folders and Freebuff sessions stay one-to-one.
- Known limit, not a blocker: two conversations with the same first message (for example "hi") share one folder. Freebuff already shares the session in that case.
- Minor: housekeeping requests (title generation) also create a scratch folder. They are harmless and empty.

@bbc About "freebuff rejects doctor": that is your machine's Freebuff build. On squire, freebuff 0.2.36 runs `freebuff doctor` correctly. Update Freebuff on chad (`npm i -g freebuff@latest`) and rerun the live answer check. Post the result here.
